@startuml skill_usage_record
' Source evidence: Java f61906b9136246ca60f333704b6fc92b5420d0ec modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeMessageEventService.java startAccepted
' Source evidence: modules/agent-core/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/agent/tool/ToolExecutionPipeline.java execute/applyAfterHook
' Source evidence: Codex d58d0e5841e0de08e251673db2d5af8cf3a1ad51 codex-rs/analytics/src/client.rs AnalyticsEventsQueue.try_send
' Observed behavior: hook failures can become tool failures; Codex analytics can drop signals.
' Design reason: catch outside the statistics transaction and retain one fact per root and Skill.
' Java divergence: bounded synchronous recording is pending implementation, not the Codex queue pipeline.
title Skill Usage Recording and Failure Isolation - Pending implementation
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
participant "Runtime input / final hook" as R
participant "Root SkillUsageTracker" as T
participant "SkillUsageService proxy" as S
database "GaussDB" as DB
note over R, T
  Explicit: input already committed, target bound, model not started.
  Read / Skill: final successful body verified against the Skill snapshot.
  No active Runtime database transaction at either entry.
end note
R -> T : qualified signal + real root + source
alt same Skill already attempted in this Tracker
  T --> R : unchanged result
else first qualified signal
  T -> T : atomically retain candidate; release memory lock
  T -> S : record(candidate)
  S -> DB : begin independent TX; Session lifecycle lock
  S -> DB : check admission and existing root / Skill fact
  alt admission closed or fact already present
    S -> DB : finish without increments
    S --> T : skipped / already recorded
  else new fact
    S -> DB : INSERT t_skill_usage
    S -> DB : increment total, then daily
    alt all statistics writes and commit succeed
      S -> DB : commit three tables
      S --> T : recorded
    else write / unique key / commit error
      S -> DB : rollback statistics when possible
      S --> T : exception after TX boundary
      T -> T : classify duplicate or failure; controlled diagnostic
    end
  end
  T --> R : unchanged result; no automatic retry
end
R -> R : continue main execution
note over T, DB
  Commit acknowledgement may be uncertain; never rerun the tool.
  Persistent PK prevents another increment after restoration.
  Missing observations are accepted; this is not an audit ledger.
end note
@enduml
